      "title": "IMF chief urges wealthy nations to tackle rising global debt levels",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/imf-chief-urges-wealthy-nations-to-tackle-rising-global-debt-levels-126101400670_1.html",
      "description": "The head of the International Monetary Fund said Wednesday that the US and other wealthy nations need to urgently tackle mounting global debt levels that are weighing heaviest on low-income countries and straining the global financial system.\nIMF Managing Director Kristalina Georgieva said that while US Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent and other US leaders recognise that the federal deficit and national debt have grown too high, just trying to grow the US economy out of its more than USD 40 trillion in national debt would not suffice.\n\"At the fund, we believe that, growth, of course, helps, but it cannot deliver fast enough the necessary adjustments,\" Georgieva said at the autumn meeting of the IMF and World Bank in Bangkok.\n\"There is no magic,\" she said, noting some other measures would be needed. \"You have to go in a direction of tightening that, bringing it down, bringing deficit down.\"\nFiscal consolidation' faces challenges\n------------------------------------------\nRising de",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-14T15:23:32"
    },
    {
      "title": "Scott Bessent's growth plans aren't enough to tame surging deficit and debt pile, IMF chief says",
      "link": "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/10/14/bond-yields-debt-deficit-treasury.html",
      "description": "IMF chief Kristalina Georgieva said Bessent’s reliance on growth won’t cut the U.S. deficit and $40 trillion debt fast enough, calling for fiscal consolidation.",
